5.953,4.941,[[28,0.974,2,472],[16,0.026,3,11]],[["0342a4da_92cd7634",14,-1,1,"Actually check header[0]?"],["194695b5_e79e2235",15,-1,1,"Any reason it's not a std::array, too, given kNoncePrefixSize exists?"],["21faf58a_256cf698",14,-1,1,"static_assert that this is < 256 might be nice?"],["59f1d07c_4c4335cc",14,-1,1,"... probably worth documenting that this is big-endian in the nice diagrams you have in the header?"],["6d80a7a6_f439dee7",15,-1,1,"... And I guess BlockIndex and Flags aren't stored? It took me a bit too realize that, so might be good to write it down."],["7f13ef4c_2d4ff842",14,-1,0,"I believe the Tink spec calls for AES-256-GCM, not AES-256-GCM-SIV: https://developers.google.com/tink/streaming-aead/aes_gcm_hkdf_streaming#encrypt_the_blocks This construction already can't reuse…"],["85b62aa8_daf57c4c",15,-1,1,"when you're implementing a spec, it makes the code clearer if the names in the code match the names in the spec as closely as possible. Tink calls this the \"key value\" so I would call it key_value."],["9963926d_de37a9ed",14,-1,1,"I think I prefer SpanWriter for this"],["a23ec5c7_7d2cf613",14,-1,1,"Seal() cannot return a too-short buffer like this when used with this cipher. I would not treat this as an error that the caller should handle via base::expected - instead I would CHECK_EQ() the…"],["a47dd485_87b68278",15,-1,1,"this comment is confusing - there is no |out_key_data|, and it's not clear why we both need to return a vector and take an out param."],["a96f8c78_3ef1f3c3",15,-1,1,"... It feels like the name needs more context than network::enterprise. Similarly for just about everything here."],["bc447d65_3c87069d",14,-1,1,"I think the preferred style these is to make it a reference and not a pointer if it can't be null. Alternatively just return it in a pair rather than have out param? That avoids a bunch of messiness…"],["cfbaba2b_6d3035be",15,0,1,"Do you really need copies?"]],0,97]]}